Terms smaller than 1e-12 in a WinMap, ShiftMap, ZoomMap or MatrixMap were treated as zero, or as equal to each other, by astSimplify and astEqual. Such terms are usual for an axis in SI units, such as a wavelength in meters or an energy in joules. As a result astSimplify could remove the shift that places the reference pixel of such an axis (a FITS header with CDELT1 = 9.425e-29 J mapped its reference pixel to the wrong energy), replace scales of 1e-26 and 3e-26 on two axes with a ZoomMap that scales both by 1e-26, and cancel a WinMap with the inverse of a different one. astEqual found any two such Mappings equal. The terms are now compared using a relative tolerance alone.
